{"lens":{"fp":"2997338152-24561","payload":"{\"score\":9,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"startup cost\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"plugin.sh runs a `$(cd ...)` subshell at load time to locate claim.sh, a fork the design decision document explicitly said to avoid by not having plugin.sh source claim.sh at all.\",\"quote\":\"_ccgl_plugin_dir=\\\"$(cd \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}\\\" 2>/dev/null || true; pwd)\\\"\",\"trigger\":\"Every time plugin.sh is loaded for the first time in a process (guarded by `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_GH_LABELS_LOADED`, so once per runner process). The design doc for this issue states: 'plugin.sh must not source core/claim/claim.sh — that would create a circular dependency and add a startup $(cd ...) subshell in plugin.sh's load path.' The code does exactly what the design said not to do.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"},{\"file\":\"core/claim/claim.sh\",\"category\":\"unnecessary subshell\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"`_ccgl_read_holder` calls `$(_ccgl_backend)` — a subshell that only echoes a variable — while the other new functions in claim.sh (`_zbuild_claim_read_labels_into`, `_zbuild_claim_add_label_direct`) explicitly replaced the same pattern with `${ZBUILD_CLAIM_BACKEND:-gh}` to avoid the fork.\",\"quote\":\"case \\\"$(_ccgl_backend)\\\" in\",\"trigger\":\"When `zbuild:claimed` is already on the issue and `zbuild_claim_acquire` calls `_ccgl_read_holder` on the conflict path; not in a hot loop, but the inconsistency is introduced here while the design comments in the same file call it out as avoided elsewhere.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]}","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"2e2649a7ef6be6c9ab172921cc93401399968c6a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"9c5e4918b9c2dd16c79aecbdd522a427e77449b0"}},"scripts/lib/run-status-re